1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,157
This is Venlix, an AI agent that rescues at-risk deliveries before they fail.

2
00:00:05,208 --> 00:00:08,317
Our XGBoost model flags risky deliveries.

3
00:00:08,287 --> 00:00:11,737
One click sends them through the LangGraph agent, concurrently.

4
00:00:11,707 --> 00:00:14,645
The live feed shows each decision as it happens.

5
00:00:15,199 --> 00:00:23,940
Six cases, eighty-three percent resolved without a human, one escalated, and ₹155 and thirty-five minutes saved.

6
00:00:24,493 --> 00:00:34,151
A traffic jam in heavy rain is classified as a driver delay, so the agent reassigns a nearby idle driver instantly, with no LLM call.

7
00:00:34,706 --> 00:00:43,169
For a gate-access problem, it texts the customer, reads the reply, extracts the new slot, tomorrow at 2 PM, and reschedules.

8
00:00:43,139 --> 00:00:44,754
Every step is traced.

9
00:00:45,307 --> 00:00:48,224
Fraud signals go straight to a human review queue.

10
00:00:48,776 --> 00:00:51,607
Ops teams can also test their own scenario.

11
00:00:51,577 --> 00:00:55,625
Pick a preset, like a wrong address, and run it through the agent live.

12
00:00:56,176 --> 00:01:02,826
The Operations Copilot answers questions over live data, like which cases were escalated, and why.

13
00:01:03,382 --> 00:01:09,968
The exception analyzer turns a messy driver note into a root cause, a fix, and similar past cases.

14
00:01:10,522 --> 00:01:13,076
The System tab shows the provider chain:

15
00:01:13,046 --> 00:01:20,379
Gemini, OpenRouter, then a built-in offline engine, which runs this entire demo without an API key.

16
00:01:20,935 --> 00:01:25,153
Venlix: fewer failed deliveries, lower costs, happier customers.

17
00:01:25,123 --> 00:01:29,447
Clone the repo and run it with one command, no API key required.

